Maria G: FYI I opened a TF change to consolidate cross-AZ NATs into a shared egress module for prod + staging. Plan link: https://ci.redwood.example/plan/6421. Need a quick config review for route_table_association, PrivateLink interaction, and secrets wiring.

Ajay K: can you paste the relevant plan diff? worried about replacement of route associations causing brief traffic loss for some subnets.

Maria G: sure - excerpt below (only the key bits):
```terraform
-/+ resource "aws_route_table_association" "app_subnet_association" {
-  subnet_id      = "subnet-0a1b2c3d"
-  route_table_id = aws_route_table.app_rt_old.id
-}
+resource "aws_route_table_association" "app_subnet_association" {
+  subnet_id      = "subnet-0a1b2c3d"
+  route_table_id = aws_route_table.app_rt_shared_eip_az1.id
+}

+resource "aws_nat_gateway" "shared" {
+  count = 3 # one per AZ
+  allocation_id = aws_eip.shared[count.index].id
+  subnet_id     = data.aws_subnet.az[count.index].id
+}
```
Notes: replacing per-subnet associations with shared route tables that point to per-AZ NAT gateways. EIP allocation will change (new EIP resources).

terraform-bot: plan created: 4 to add, 3 to change, 2 to destroy. Lock acquired on backend s3://redwood-terraform-state/infra.tfstate.

Chloe P: Will this break PrivateLink interface endpoints in analytics/recv subnets? Those need to remain reachable and use ENIs.

Maria G: Good call — the interface endpoints stay in-place. We update the route table attached to those subnets to keep local VPC routes plus endpoints. PrivateLink traffic is interface ENIs -> doesn't traverse NAT, but DNS/private hosted zone forwarding needs to keep the same resolver. I'm adding a small `aws_route_table` exception for endpoint subnets so we don't route 10.0.0.0/8 to NAT by mistake.

Ben R: Make sure tfstate lock/consistency is enforced and do a staged apply. Do not run a full prod apply without a canary. Suggest: apply to staging (same AZs) with `-target=module.egress` then run smoke tests. Also double-check IGW vs NAT route priority (we had an incident when IGW leaked).

Ajay K: also watch out for on-prem BGP paths — our route propagation to the TGW had a fallback to IGW in one case. Any changes to `aws_route` with `destination_cidr_block = "0.0.0.0/0"` need review.

Maria G: acknowledged. I'm keeping separate route tables: `rt-app-shared-eip-az*` for egress, `rt-endpoints` for privatelink. I'll run the staging canary at 2pm PT and post logs.

Chloe P: nit: in the module, prefer `create_before_destroy = true` for `aws_eip` to avoid losing addresses during attach. Also add a short wait_for (sleep) after NAT creation before flipping associations.

Maria G: good call — adding lifecycle + a `null_resource` with local-exec sleep 30s between create and assoc:```hcl
resource "aws_eip" "shared" {
  count = var.az_count
  vpc   = true
  lifecycle { create_before_destroy = true }
}

resource "null_resource" "pause_before_assoc" {
  triggers = { nat_ids = join(",", aws_nat_gateway.shared.*.id) }
  provisioner "local-exec" { command = "sleep 30" }
}```

infra-bot: reminder: please add a PR description with the rollback steps and the expected TF plan counts for prod before merging.

Maria G: done — PR now has rollback steps (reassociate previous RTs, reattach old EIPs) and a pre-check doc for smoke tests. Also updating SSM param `egress/eip-prod` via a small module so ops can rotate if needed.

Ajay K: LGTM from networking side pending the canary. I'll join the apply watch. :eyes:

Chloe P: +1, just ensure PrivateLink owners (svc-analytics) accept the endpoint service if we need to change the service owner for cross-account acceptance.

Maria G: will coordinate. If anyone wants to shadow the staging apply ping me and I'll invite you to the apply channel. Thanks all :thumbsup:

Ben R: Thanks — ping infra on-call if anything unexpected pops up during the apply.

Maria G: will do, closing the loop after staging verify.
